course: dictionary
lesson: 12349
title: Crave: a very strong wish
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To crave something means to want it very strongly, so much that it is hard to think about anything else. «After the long swim, Ben craved a cold drink.» Ben did not just want a drink. He wanted one badly.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «Mia craves attention, so she waves and shouts in every game.» Ask yourself what would fit in place of craves. "Wants a lot" fits, so crave means want very strongly.
explain: Crave can also be old and formal. In old stories, a person might crave a favour from a king, which means asking for it humbly. «I crave your pardon» means «please forgive me». Words like «your pardon» tell you it is an old-fashioned, polite use.
explain: Health lessons use craving too. A craving is a strong wish, often for sugar or salty food. «I have a craving for crisps» means you want crisps very much.
fact: Crave is a verb: I crave, he craves, she craved, craving.
fact: «Crave» means to want something very strongly.
fact: «Craving» is the noun: a strong wish, as in «a craving for sweets».
fact: In old, formal language, «crave» means to ask for something humbly, as in «I crave your pardon».
fact: A lonely character in a story may crave friendship.
exercise: «After the long swim, Ben craved a cold drink.» What does craved mean? | *Wanted very strongly | Spilled carelessly | Forgot about completely | Shared happily
exercise: In «She had a craving for salty crisps», what is a craving? | *A strong wish | A long walk | A kind of crisp | A large bowl
exercise: Lily craves friendship at her new school. What does Lily want most? | *Friends who like her | To be alone all day | A new bicycle | A bigger bedroom
test: «The lonely king craved a friend to talk to.» What does craved mean here? | *Wanted very strongly | Finished | Hated | Ignored
test: In old language, «I crave your pardon» means: | I am sure you are wrong | I want you to leave now | *I humbly ask you to forgive me | I have lost your book
exam: «Our team craved victory all season.» What does this show? | The team was tired of playing | The team had already won | *The team wanted to win very badly | The team did not care about the result
